do GameState.start_minigame()
[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_1.png" fade="1.0" transition="Push Up"]
audio music "res://audio/higheruniversalman-take-me-out-to-the-ball-game-sports-stadium-crowd-music-506221.mp3" [volume="-14.0" loop="true"]
join Dagger (Full Body) center
[wait time="1.5"]
Dagger: [that conversation i overheard just now is very compelling...]
set {strikes_number} += 1.0
jump Ball
label Journal Select
do MenuManager.open_journal()
[wait_input]
if {is_success} == true:
	do MinegameTest.update_background("strikes_number")
	if {current_item} == "d_brother_death":
		Lizzy: you told me last loop that your first vampire kill was your older brother.
		Dagger: Oh.
		Dagger: that is not something I ever wished to share with you, Elizabeth.
		Lizzy: you were in a pretty bad place. Yeah.
		Dagger: My brother wasn't a good person, but he did not deserve his fate. I atone for that mistake everyday-
		Lizzy: yeah youve told me all this already.
		Dagger: oh, yes, that makes sense.
	elif {current_item} == "d_zombie_plan":
		Lizzy: For the last few loops Lady MacDeath keeps attacking the town with zombies.
		Lizzy: it's really annoying.
		Dagger: her plan... how could you possibly know that. I haven't told you yet.
		Lizzy: i also know that she's doing it because she's really broken up about me killing her husband. Like really broken up.
		Dagger: yes. She hasn't been herself lately.
		Lizzy: uh, she seems the same sort of crazy as she was before?
		Dagger: She isn't so bad once you get to know her. She can be quite lovely at times. Shakespeare was her husbands thing, and honestly, she sort of hates the bard.
		do GameState.learn_fact("m_shakespeare_hate")
		Dagger: i think that eventually she will come into her own, but for now, she's using it as a critch to deal with her negative emotions.
		Lizzy: youve really analysed her, huh?
		Dagger: i spend a lot of time alone with my thoughts
		Lizzy: well now shes added time loop to her ultimate revenge plan,  so that's great.
		Dagger: i dont know why she wouldnt have talked to me about it first. She always consults me before her evil plans.
		Lizzy: conflict of interest?
		Dagger: I suppose she's noticed how frequently we've been speaking.
	set {strikes_number} += 1.0
	label Ball
	join Item leftmost [animation="Zoom In" length="9.0"]
	leave Item [animation="Slide To Right" length="1.1" wait="true"]
	if {strikes_number} == 1.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_2.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	elif {strikes_number} == 2.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_3.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	elif {strikes_number} == 3.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_4.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	[wait time="1.5"]
else:
	Dagger: And this is supposed to mean something to me because....?
	Lizzy: Uh... I was just testing to see if you're paying attention.
	[V.O] I'll have to try something else.
set {is_success} = false
if {strikes_number} < 3.0:
	jump Journal Select
[background fade="2.0" wait="true"]
audio music - [fade="4.0"]
Dagger: it doesn't make any sense...
leave --All-- [animation="Fade Out Down" wait="true"]
do GameState.end_minigame()
jump ending_5/